{"slug":"hero","title":"The groove","blurb":"Horn stabs cut from an 1889 Sousa march, over a kit of drum one-shots, warped and tuned, with a different rhythm every bar.","score":"examples/hero.apr","code":"# Hero \u2014 the landing-page groove: the horns of Sousa's The Thunderer (1889), sliced into four\n# stabs on a four-on-the-floor pulse, over the Salamander Drumkit (CC BY-SA 3.0, Alexander Holm).\n# Everything plays from bar 1; every bar is a different rhythm instead of a build-up.\n# Fetch the kit with: apricity sources fetch salamander-drumkit\ntempo 104\nkey F mixolydian\nsamples ../samples\n\nclip horns    = marine-band/stems/Thunderer/other.wav  beats 14..18   # four beats whose attacks land on the beat (within 9 ms)\n\n# One-shots are re-pitched: they play as recorded, never stretched to the grid.\nclip kick     = salamander-drumkit/OH/kick_OH_F_1.wav         warp repitch\nclip snare    = salamander-drumkit/OH/snare_OH_F_1.wav        warp repitch\nclip ghost    = salamander-drumkit/OH/snare_OH_Ghost_1.wav    warp repitch\nclip stick    = salamander-drumkit/OH/snareStick_OH_F_1.wav   warp repitch\nclip hat      = salamander-drumkit/OH/hihatClosed_OH_F_1.wav  warp repitch\nclip open     = salamander-drumkit/OH/hihatOpen_OH_F_1.wav    warp repitch\nclip tom      = salamander-drumkit/OH/hiTom_OH_F_1.wav        warp repitch\nclip floor    = salamander-drumkit/OH/loTom_OH_MP_1.wav       warp repitch\nclip crash    = salamander-drumkit/OH/crash1_OH_FF_1.wav      warp repitch\n\nkit h = slice horns by beats 1         # four stabs, one per beat, each starting on a note attack\n\nkit drums\n  kick  = kick\n  snare = snare\n  ghost = ghost\n  stick = stick\n  hat   = hat\n  open  = open\n  tom   = tom\n  floor = floor\n  crash = crash\n\nchords I7 . IV7 . | I7 . V7 IV7\n\n# Horn stabs on every beat, a different order and push each bar.\ntrack h  steps \"1 _ _ _ 2 _ _ _ 3 _ _ _ 4 _ _ _ | 1 _ _ 1 _ _ 2 _ . . 3 _ 4 _ _ _ | 1 _ . 3 _ . 1 _ 2 _ _ _ 4 _ 2 _ | 3 _ _ _ 3 _ . . 1 _ 2 _ 4 _ _ _ | 1 _ _ _ 2 _ _ _ 3 _ . 3 4 _ _ _ | 2 _ . 1 _ . 2 _ 1 _ _ _ 4 _ . 3 | 1 _ _ _ 3 _ 1 _ 2 _ . 2 _ . 4 _ | 4 _ _ _ 3 _ _ _ 2 _ _ _ 1 _ 1 1\"  follow  filter hp 250  volume -1\n\n# Kick on every beat (with a pushed kick in some bars); the snare backbeat, with ghosts, sticks and\n# tom fills changing bar to bar.\ntrack drums.kick  steps \"x _ _ _ x _ _ _ x _ _ _ x _ _ _ | x _ _ _ x _ _ _ x _ _ x x _ _ _ | x _ _ _ x _ _ _ x _ _ _ x _ _ _ | x _ _ _ x _ _ _ x _ _ _ x _ x _ | x _ _ _ x _ _ _ x _ _ _ x _ _ _ | x _ _ x x _ _ _ x _ _ _ x _ _ _ | x _ _ _ x _ _ _ x _ x _ x _ _ _ | x _ _ _ x _ _ _ x _ _ _ x _ _ _\"  volume +1\ntrack drums  steps \". . . . snare _ _ _ . . . . snare _ _ _ | . . . ghost snare _ _ _ . . ghost . snare _ _ ghost | . . . . snare _ _ stick . . . stick snare _ _ _ | . . . . snare _ ghost . . . . . snare _ tom floor | . . . . snare _ _ _ . . . ghost snare _ ghost . | . . ghost . snare _ _ _ . . . . snare _ stick stick | . . . . snare _ _ ghost . . ghost . snare _ _ _ | . . . . snare _ _ _ . . tom tom floor floor [snare snare] [snare snare]\"  volume -9\n\n# Hats: straight eighths, sixteenths, and open hats on the off-beats, a different figure each bar.\ntrack drums.hat   steps \". . x . . . x . . . x . . . x . | x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x | . . x . . . x . . . x . . . x x | x . x . x . x . x . x . x . x . | . . x . . . x . . . x . . . x . | x x x . x x x . x x x . x x x . | . . x . . . x x . . x . . . x . | x . x . x . x . x . x . . . . .\"  volume -9\ntrack drums.open  steps \". . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . | . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . | . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . | . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . | . . x . . . x . . . x . . . x . | . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . | . . . . . . . . . . x . . . . . | . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .\"  gate 50%  volume -22\ntrack drums.crash  at 1 5  volume -22\n","provenance":[{"source":"h","title":"The Thunderer \u2014 horns","kind":"loop","tracks":["h"],"recordings":[{"title":"The Thunderer","part":"horns","composed":1889,"recorded":"2017","performer":"\"The President's Own\" United States Marine Band","credit":"\"The President's Own\" United States Marine Band, The Complete Marches of John Philip Sousa, Vol. 3.","rights":"Public domain (composition pre-1923; recording is a work of the U.S. Government).","licence":"Public domain","source_page":"https://www.marineband.marines.mil/Audio-Resources/The-Complete-Marches-of-John-Philip-Sousa/The-Thunderer-March/","parts":["horns"]}]},{"source":"drums","title":"Salamander Drumkit \u2014 drums","kind":"kit","tracks":["drums.kick","drums","drums.hat","drums.open","drums.crash"],"recordings":[{"title":"Salamander Drumkit","part":null,"composed":null,"recorded":null,"performer":null,"credit":"Alexander Holm, Salamander Drumkit (Internet Archive).","rights":"CC BY-SA 3.0, Alexander Holm; share-alike applies if you modify the samples. https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","source_page":"https://archive.org/details/SalamanderDrumkit","parts":[]}]}],"captions":{},"audio":{"sources":["breakdowns/hero/h-source.mp3","breakdowns/hero/drums-source.mp3"],"tracks":[{"key":"breakdowns/hero/h-track.mp3","gain_db":-3.6},{"key":"breakdowns/hero/drums-track.mp3","gain_db":-3.3}]},"tempo":104.0,"meter":4,"key":"F mixolydian","beats":32.0,"chords":[{"start":0.0,"end":8.0,"numeral":"I7","name":"F7"},{"start":8.0,"end":16.0,"numeral":"IV7","name":"Bb7"},{"start":16.0,"end":24.0,"numeral":"I7","name":"F7"},{"start":24.0,"end":28.0,"numeral":"V7","name":"C7"},{"start":28.0,"end":32.0,"numeral":"IV7","name":"Bb7"}],"sources":[{"id":"h","title":"The Thunderer \u2014 horns","credit":"composed 1889 \u00b7 recorded 2017 by \"The President's Own\" United States Marine Band \u00b7 horns stem","kind":"loop","path":"audio/smp_971760bb9da19b437bd0/other.wav","window":[5.3,11.3],"peaks":"","beats":[5.3,5.82,6.3,6.8,7.3,7.8,8.3,8.8,9.3,9.78,10.28,10.56,10.8,11.06,11.3],"downbeats":[6.3,8.3,10.28,11.3],"tran